                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Valve added realistic physics to Counter-Strike, and the community immediately used them to turn the game into a playground for absolute degenerates.\n\nBeautiful.\n\nCounter-Strike: Source brought improved visuals, satisfying gunplay, and the glorious chaos of Source Engine physics. But the real magic was always the community servers. Zombie Escape, Surf, Deathrun, custom maps... You could spend an entire evening playing Counter-Strike without actually playing Counter-Strike.\n\nOf course, not everything was perfect. The shooting never felt quite as precise as 1.6, hit registration could be frustrating, and the competitive experience wasn't everyone's favourite.\n\nHas it aged well? Surprisingly well. The graphics are dated, but the gameplay remains enjoyable, and its community-created content still gives it a personality that modern matchmaking struggles to replicate.\n\nRatings:\n\nGameplay: 8.5/10\n\nGraphics: 7/10\n\nCommunity & Custom Content: 10/10\n\nReplayability: 9/10\n\nEnjoyment: 9/10\n\nCS 1.6 was the competitive legend. CS: Source was the unhinged cousin who discovered physics and never recovered.\n\nOverall: 8.5/10 | Recommended",
